### Task 1.5 - mesas do restaurante
### Ambiente: selecione "dev" no IntelliJ HTTP Client, com http-client.env.json
### + http-client.private.env.json (copie o .example). Ver http/README.md.
###
### Pre-requisito: aplicacao rodando no perfil "dev" com o seed habilitado.
### Rode o arquivo inteiro, em ordem: os cenarios do caminho feliz salvam os ids
### que os cenarios negativos usam.
###
### A identificacao da mesa leva um sufixo aleatorio porque e unica por
### propriedade, ignorando maiusculas: sem isso, a segunda execucao bateria em
### 409. As listas sao filtradas pelo sufixo, para ignorar mesas de execucoes
### anteriores.


### 0. Login do admin
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{adminUsername}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

> {%
    client.test("login do admin retorna 200", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, recebido " + response.status);
    });
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("suffix", Math.random().toString(36).substring(2, 8));
%}


### 1. Cria a Mesa 10 no Salao
POST {{host}}/api/restaurant/dining-tables
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "Mesa 10 {{suffix}}",
  "seats": 4,
  "area": "Salao"
}

> {%
    client.test("mesa criada retorna 201, ativa", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "esperado 201, recebido " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.seats === 4, "seats deveria ser 4");
        client.assert(response.body.area === "Salao", "area deveria ser Salao");
        client.assert(response.body.isActive === true, "mesa nasce ativa");
    });
    client.global.set("table10Id", response.body.id);
%}


### 2. Cria a Mesa 2 no Salao, com espacos a aparar
POST {{host}}/api/restaurant/dining-tables
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "  Mesa 2 {{suffix}}  ",
  "seats": 2,
  "area": "  Salao  "
}

> {%
    client.test("mesa criada com identificacao e area aparadas", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "esperado 201, recebido " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.label === "Mesa 2 " + client.global.get("suffix"), "label deveria vir aparado");
        client.assert(response.body.area === "Salao", "area deveria vir aparada");
    });
    client.global.set("table2Id", response.body.id);
%}


### 3. Cria a V1 na Varanda
POST {{host}}/api/restaurant/dining-tables
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "V1 {{suffix}}",
  "seats": 6,
  "area": "Varanda"
}

> {%
    client.test("V1 criada retorna 201", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "esperado 201, recebido " + response.status);
    });
    client.global.set("verandaTableId", response.body.id);
%}


### 4. Cria uma mesa sem lugares e com area em branco
POST {{host}}/api/restaurant/dining-tables
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "Balcao {{suffix}}",
  "area": "   "
}

> {%
    client.test("mesa sem area retorna 201 com seats e area nulos", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "esperado 201, recebido " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.seats === null, "seats deveria ser null");
        client.assert(response.body.area === null, "area em branco deveria virar null");
    });
%}


### 5. Lista: por area (sem area por ultimo), depois ordem natural
GET {{host}}/api/restaurant/dining-tables
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

> {%
    const suffix = client.global.get("suffix");
    const labels = response.body.map(function(table) { return table.label; })
        .filter(function(label) { return label.endsWith(" " + suffix); });
    client.test("lista ordenada: Mesa 2, Mesa 10, V1, Balcao", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, recebido " + response.status);
        client.assert(JSON.stringify(labels) === JSON.stringify(["Mesa 2 " + suffix, "Mesa 10 " + suffix, "V1 " + suffix, "Balcao " + suffix]), "ordem recebida: " + JSON.stringify(labels));
    });
%}


### 6. Le uma mesa
GET {{host}}/api/restaurant/dining-tables/{{table10Id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

> {%
    client.test("mesa lida retorna 200", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, recebido " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.label === "Mesa 10 " + client.global.get("suffix"), "label deveria ser Mesa 10");
    });
%}


### 7. Edita a V1: cadastro inteiro, sem seats limpa os lugares
PUT {{host}}/api/restaurant/dining-tables/{{verandaTableId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "V1 {{suffix}}",
  "area": "Varanda coberta"
}

> {%
    client.test("edicao substitui o cadastro inteiro", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, recebido " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.seats === null, "seats ausente deveria limpar os lugares");
        client.assert(response.body.area === "Varanda coberta", "area deveria ser Varanda coberta");
    });
%}


### 8. Edita mudando so a caixa da propria identificacao
PUT {{host}}/api/restaurant/dining-tables/{{verandaTableId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "label": "v1 {{suffix}}",
  "area": "Varanda"
}

> {%
    client.test("a mesa nao concorre com ela mesma", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, recebido " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.label === "v1 " + client.global.get("suffix"), "label deveria ser guardado como digitado");
    });
%}


### 9. Desativa a V1
POST {{host}}/api/restaurant/dining-tables/{{verandaTableId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

> {%
    client.test("mesa desativada", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, recebido " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.isActive === false, "mesa deveria estar inativa");
    });
%}


### 10. Desativa de novo: idempotente
POST {{host}}/api/restaurant/dining-tables/{{verandaTableId}}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

> {%
    client.test("desativar de novo e aceito", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, recebido " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.isActive === false, "mesa continua inativa");
    });
%}


### 11. Lista padrao: so as ativas
GET {{host}}/api/restaurant/dining-tables
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

> {%
    const suffix = client.global.get("suffix");
    const labels = response.body.map(function(table) { return table.label; })
        .filter(function(label) { return label.endsWith(" " + suffix); });
    client.test("lista padrao sem a V1", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, recebido " + response.status);
        client.assert(JSON.stringify(labels) === JSON.stringify(["Mesa 2 " + suffix, "Mesa 10 " + suffix, "Balcao " + suffix]), "ordem recebida: " + JSON.stringify(labels));
    });
%}


### 12. Lista com as inativas
GET {{host}}/api/restaurant/dining-tables?includeInactive=true
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

> {%
    const suffix = client.global.get("suffix");
    const labels = response.body.map(function(table) { return table.label; })
        .filter(function(label) { return label.endsWith(" " + suffix); });
    client.test("lista com inativas traz a V1 no lugar dela", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, recebido " + response.status);
        client.assert(JSON.stringify(labels) === JSON.stringify(["Mesa 2 " + suffix, "Mesa 10 " + suffix, "v1 " + suffix, "Balcao " + suffix]), "ordem recebida: " + JSON.stringify(labels));
    });
%}


### 13. Reativa a V1
POST {{host}}/api/restaurant/dining-tables/{{verandaTableId}}/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

> {%
    client.test("mesa reativada", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "esperado 200, recebido " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.isActive === true, "mesa deveria estar ativa");
    });
%}


### ------------------------------------------------------------------
### Cenarios negativos: um por codigo de erro
### ------------------------------------------------------------------


### 14. Mesa inexistente -> 404 DINING_TABLE_NOT_FOUND
GET {{host}}/api/restaurant/dining-tables/00000000-0000-0000-0000-0000000000ff
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

> {%
    client.test("mesa inexistente retorna 404", function() {
        client.assert(response.status === 404, "esperado 404, recebido " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.code === "DINING_TABLE_NOT_FOUND", "code deveria ser DINING_TABLE_NOT_FOUND");
    });
%}


